            <ArticleTitle>Management of venous and cardiovascular thrombosis: enoxaparin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>628-36</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enoxaparin has strong clinical evidence that supports its license in a broad spectrum of therapeutic indications, including thromboprophylaxis in surgical patients, medical patients bedridden because of acute illness, the once-daily treatment of venous thromboembolism and the treatment of unstable angina and non-Q wave myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
